    size cx=R:[si] and a byte-pair w=R:[si+2] (bx = lo(w)*hi(w)); emit a 4-word descriptor
    {data_off, R, bx+data_off, bx} to the output table at (word[DGROUP:0x4f0]):out_off; advance si by
    the entry size, wrapping the segment by +0x800 when si crosses 0x8000; store the entry count to
    R(orig):2 when a zero size terminates the chain (bail if out_off reaches 0x1630).
The c388 return CF (asm `jae` past the ret) is a documented residual flag-thread class; the pristine
decompile hardcoded "continue" and the boot-path resources open OK, so it is kept as continue.
